TITLE:: Smear
summary:: a spectral processor that freezes, blurs, scrambles, shifts and combs the sound, as a UGen and as an object, with a window
categories:: Libraries>Smear
related:: Classes/FxParamUnit, Classes/SmearView, Classes/FxUnit, Classes/FxChain

DESCRIPTION::
A spectral processor - freeze, blur, scramble, shift, comb - running anywhere a UGen does, with a window.

code::
Ndef(\voice, { Smear.ar(Saw.ar([110, 111]) * LFPulse.kr(2).lag(0.01) * 0.2, \smear) }).play;

m = Smear(Ndef(\voice), \smear);
m.gui;
m.frozen = true;                  // hold it
m.frozen = false;
m.preset = 'glass choir';
m.smear = 12; m.shift = 16;
::

The sound is taken apart with an FFT and bent, all of it with SuperCollider's own PV UGens. In order: hold the spectrum (code::frozen::, or stepped by code::hold::), move it (code::shift::), average neighbours (code::smear::), swap bins (code::scramble::), take random bins away (code::holes::), take evenly spaced teeth away (code::teeth::), pass only what is over a level (code::gate::), and cut from one end (code::brick::). All neutral, the wet is the input to within 0.01 dB.

Two of those needed more than the UGen. code::PV_MagFreeze:: holds magnitudes but takes its phases from the input, and silence has none to give, so a held note would turn into a buzz at the frame rate. While held, the FFT hears the last moment of sound looped instead. code::PV_BinShift:: on its own cancels against itself, 66 dB down on a sine, so a phase correction goes with it and code::shift:: moves in whole bins, about 23 Hz each.

code::stretch:: multiplies every partial, which is a pitch shift. It is code::PitchShift:: ahead of the FFT, so it keeps the shift's own graininess and adds 100 ms; a pure tone comes out about 5 dB down with sidebands around it.

It costs the FFT's latency, 2048 frames less a block: about 41 ms at 48 kHz. The dry is delayed by as much, so code::mix:: lines up, and the latency stays while it is in the graph, bypassed or not.

subsection:: The object and the UGen
It is an link::Classes/FxParamUnit::, so everything that class documents works here: code::Smear.ar(in, name)::, code::Smear(node, name)::, code::Smear.onBus(bus, numChannels)::, presets, the clipboard, code::gui::. Its window's display is a link::Classes/SmearView::.

subsection:: Parameters
Each is a property of the object: read it, set it. The numbers are in the order of the node's control, which is what saved node maps carry. Internal ones without a knob, if any, are described above.

table::
## strong::parameter:: || strong::range:: || strong::default:: || strong::what it does::
## code::frozen:: || on / off || false || hold this spectrum, for as long as it is on
## code::hold:: || 0 .. 30 Hz || 0 || take a new spectrum this often and hold it in between: 0 is off
## code::smear:: || 0 .. 64 bins || 0 || how many bins each side are averaged in
## code::scramble:: || 0 .. 1 || 0 || how many bins are swapped
## code::scrambleWidth:: || 0.01 .. 1 || 0.2 || how far apart they may be
## code::scrambleRate:: || 0.1 .. 30 Hz || 4 || how often a new order is drawn
## code::diffuse:: || on / off || false || new phases, from time to time: transients wash away
## code::shift:: || -256 .. 256 bins || 0 || add this many bins to every partial, about 23 Hz each: harmonics stop being harmonics
## code::stretch:: || 0.25 .. 4 x || 1 || multiply every partial: a pitch shift, with its own 100 ms of delay
## code::holes:: || 0 .. 1 || 0 || how many bins are taken away at random
## code::holesRate:: || 0.1 .. 30 Hz || 2 || how often new ones are drawn
## code::teeth:: || 0 .. 48 || 0 || how many teeth are taken out of the spectrum: 0 is none
## code::combWidth:: || 0.02 .. 0.98 || 0.5 || how much of each tooth passes
## code::combRate:: || 0 .. 8 Hz || 0.25 || how quickly the teeth move
## code::gate:: || -96 .. 0 dB || -96 || only what is over this comes through: the loudest partials
## code::brick:: || -1 .. 1 || 0 || under 0 takes the top of the spectrum off, over 0 the bottom
## code::width:: || 0 .. 2 || 1 || how far apart the sides are
## code::mix:: || 0 .. 1 || 1 || how much of the effect goes out, against the dry signal
## code::output:: || -36 .. 24 dB || 0 || the level of the whole thing, in dB
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: fftSize
the frames in a frame: 2048. Change it before the def is built.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

EXAMPLES::

code::
s.boot;
Ndef(\voice, { Smear.ar(Saw.ar([110, 111]) * LFPulse.kr(2).lag(0.01) * 0.2, \smear) }).play;
m = Smear(Ndef(\voice), \smear);
m.gui;
m.preset = Smear.presetNames.choose;
m.free; Ndef(\voice).clear;
::
